    "body": "@ved-rivos I like the idea, but this to me is strictly orthogonal to the speculation barrier instruction proposal.  I suggest separating this into a  different extension name and document.  One motivation for doing so is to expedite the RISC-V standardization processes around the Zisb barrier instructions, to try to minimize a riotous explosion of unnecessary software complexity as different vendors implement their own custom barriers in the absence of clear guidance from RVI.\r\n\r\nI also believe that this is a better fit to be associated with the temporal fence work.  As I read the current fence.time proposal, a practical effect of your proposal would be to reduce the performance impact of fence.time with the PRIV_SWITCH, AS_SWITCH, or VM_SWITCH flags, since they would effectively become no-ops.  There would need to be a new instruction from that group, or new fence.time flags needed, to indicate identifier reuse, which is where I think @radimkrcmar was going.\r\n\r\nIncidentally, the Zifencetime strawman https://github.com/riscv-admin/timing-fences/blob/main/extension/Zifencetime.adoc discusses the partitioning idea in the current text.\r\n",
